{"code":"PhT","title":"The Phoenix and the Turtle","kind":"poem","units":[{"label":"","scenes":[{"label":"1","entries":[{"t":"text","lines":[{"n":"1","text":"Let the bird of loudest lay"},{"n":"2","text":"On the sole Arabian tree"},{"n":"3","text":"Herald sad and trumpet be,"},{"n":"4","text":"To whose sound chaste wings obey."},{"n":"5","text":"But thou shrieking harbinger,"},{"n":"6","text":"Foul precurrer of the fiend,"},{"n":"7","text":"Augur of the fever’s end,"},{"n":"8","text":"To this troop come thou not near."},{"n":"9","text":"From this session interdict"},{"n":"10","text":"Every fowl of tyrant wing,"},{"n":"11","text":"Save the eagle, feathered king;"},{"n":"12","text":"Keep the obsequy so strict."},{"n":"13","text":"Let the priest in surplice white,"},{"n":"14","text":"That defunctive music can,"},{"n":"15","text":"Be the death-divining swan,"},{"n":"16","text":"Lest the requiem lack his right."},{"n":"17","text":"And thou treble-dated crow,"},{"n":"18","text":"That thy sable gender mak’st"},{"n":"19","text":"With the breath thou giv’st and tak’st,"},{"n":"20","text":"’Mongst our mourners shalt thou go."},{"n":"21","text":"Here the anthem doth commence:"},{"n":"22","text":"Love and constancy is dead,"},{"n":"23","text":"Phoenix and the turtle fled"},{"n":"24","text":"In a mutual flame from hence."},{"n":"25","text":"So they loved, as love in twain"},{"n":"26","text":"Had the essence but in one,"},{"n":"27","text":"Two distincts, division none;"},{"n":"28","text":"Number there in love was slain."},{"n":"29","text":"Hearts remote yet not asunder,"},{"n":"30","text":"Distance and no space was seen"},{"n":"31","text":"’Twixt this turtle and his queen;"},{"n":"32","text":"But in them it were a wonder."},{"n":"33","text":"So between them love did shine"},{"n":"34","text":"That the turtle saw his right"},{"n":"35","text":"Flaming in the phoenix’ sight;"},{"n":"36","text":"Either was the other’s mine."},{"n":"37","text":"Property was thus appalled"},{"n":"38","text":"That the self was not the same;"},{"n":"39","text":"Single nature’s double name"},{"n":"40","text":"Neither two nor one was called."},{"n":"41","text":"Reason, in itself confounded,"},{"n":"42","text":"Saw division grow together,"},{"n":"43","text":"To themselves yet either neither,"},{"n":"44","text":"Simple were so well compounded"},{"n":"45","text":"That it cried, How true a twain"},{"n":"46","text":"Seemeth this concordant one!"},{"n":"47","text":"Love hath reason, Reason none,"},{"n":"48","text":"If what parts can so remain,"},{"n":"49","text":"Whereupon it made this threne"},{"n":"50","text":"To the phoenix and the dove,"},{"n":"51","text":"Co-supremes and stars of love,"},{"n":"52","text":"As chorus to their tragic scene. Threnos"},{"n":"53","text":"Beauty, truth, and rarity,"},{"n":"54","text":"Grace in all simplicity,"},{"n":"55","text":"Here enclosed, in cinders lie."},{"n":"56","text":"Death is now the phoenix’ nest,"},{"n":"57","text":"And the turtle’s loyal breast"},{"n":"58","text":"To eternity doth rest,"},{"n":"59","text":"Leaving no posterity;"},{"n":"60","text":"’Twas not their infirmity,"},{"n":"61","text":"It was married chastity."},{"n":"62","text":"Truth may seem, but cannot be;"},{"n":"63","text":"Beauty brag, but ’tis not she;"},{"n":"64","text":"Truth and beauty buried be."},{"n":"65","text":"To this urn let those repair"},{"n":"66","text":"That are either true or fair;"},{"n":"67","text":"For these dead birds sigh a prayer."}]}]}]}],"characters":[],"lineCount":67}